new file mode 100644
index 0000000..82bf729
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Marginalia Books
+
+A fictional independent bookshop website: four pages (home, books, events, visit)
+in plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. There is no build step and no npm dependency
+for the site itself. Nothing is loaded from a CDN, web font, or remote image.
+
+## Pages
+
+- `index.html`: intro, staff picks, next events, hours and address summary
+- `books.html`: catalogue with a genre filter kept in the URL (`?genre=mystery`)
+- `events.html`: upcoming events, and past events in their own section
+- `visit.html`: opening hours with today highlighted, address, access notes and a contact form
+
+The catalogue, events and opening hours live in `js/data.js`. Addresses, the
+footer and the visit copy live in the HTML pages, so edit those there.
+
+## Run it
+
+The pages use `defer` scripts and can be opened directly from disk, but serving
+them is the easiest way to check them. From the repository root, run either:
+
+```sh
+npx http-server . -p 8080
+```
+
+or
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8080
+```
+
+Then open <http://localhost:8080/>.
+
+## Test it
+
+The browser tests drive the real pages in headless Chrome through Playwright.
+They use the system Chrome at `/usr/bin/google-chrome` and start their own local
+static server, so no server needs to be running first.
+
+```sh
+NODE_PATH=/opt/node22/lib/node_modules node tests/site.test.cjs
+```
+
+To run a subset of tests by name, pass `--grep`:
+
+```sh
+NODE_PATH=/opt/node22/lib/node_modules node tests/site.test.cjs --grep AC5
+```
+
+The suite exits non-zero if any test fails.
